81: ## Producer inventory required before implementation
82: 
83: For each row, identify the selected emission rule, its result representation,
84: its binding/flow dependencies, and the next consumer. Existing compiler support
85: and source-language acceptance are separate evidence. An unverified path stays
86: open; it cannot be removed from the accepted language to simplify this pilot.
87: 
88: | Producer family | Required representation owner and review evidence |
89: | --- | --- |
90: | Local, field, and parameter read | Selected declaration and read representation; parameter body normalization and current guard facts are explicit. Cover inferred declarations and optional field reads. |
91: | Literal and construction | The selected target constructor determines storage. Null and contextual empty literals retain their distinct identities until materialization. Audit built-in array construction separately from constructors that cannot return an array. |
92: | Ordinary and specialized call | Emitted callable return representation, or the selected intrinsic/helper operation when it replaces a call. A source return annotation alone does not certify a replaced operation. |
93: | Cast and completed conversion | Consume the inner prepared result and return the conversion plan's result. Parentheses and metadata preserve that result; a contextual cast does not erase its actual storage. |
94: | Ordinary conditional | Prepare each arm under its branch environment and reconcile reachable results to one representation. Return the joined facts. |
95: | Structural nil-merge | One shared structural decision selects the guarded value and lazy fallback. Both operands participate in representation selection. |
96: | Registered default | Declaration/body plan and selected default operation establish the result. Registration or native-default placement alone proves no presence. |
97: | Block tail | Statement scope and tail producer determine the returned value, including any generated closure or temporary. Preserve its result representation at the enclosing boundary. |
98: | Switch result and pattern binding | Audit expression, assignment, and return lowering routes, destination temporaries, arm results, and payload declarations. |
99: | Try result | Audit `tryBindingLines`, return paths, and statement paths. Rejection in the generic expression dispatcher does not establish source-domain exclusion. |
100: | Nested collection element | The element producer/conversion supplies the element representation; the outer constructor independently supplies the container representation. |
101: 
